      "innovation": "Joint optimization of text and vision: early vision fusion with a constant token ratio throughout training; explains that mixing tokens early yields better results than late fusion; differs from conventional approaches that add visual tokens at a late stage. Zero-vision SFT: text-only supervised fine-tuning activates visual reasoning and tool use; explains that joint pre-training establishes strong alignment so visual data isn't needed at SFT; differs from prior methods that require visual trajectories at SFT. Joint text-vision RL: reinforcement learning applied to both modalities simultaneously; explains bidirectional enhancement where text bootstraps vision and vision refines text; differs from unimodal RL. Agent Swarm & PARL: parallel agent orchestration framework with a Parallel-Agent Reinforcement Learning paradigm; explains freezing sub-agents and updating only the orchestrator via verifiable rewards; differs from sequential execution and end-to-end co-optimization to avoid credit assignment ambiguity and training instability.",
